    "DefaultText": "A dugout canoe hollowed from a tree log, its seams patched with bark. On a flowing river it carries you and your load all the way down to Brackwater Mouth, the river's end, in about an hour. It cannot be paddled upstream, on a lake, a marsh or a frozen river, and it is heavy to carry."
  },
